<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — STREAM AUTH" description="Privacy policy for the Stream Auth software authentication platform." path="/privacy"><article class="legal shell"><p class="eyebrow">LEGAL</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="legal-date">Last updated: July 30, 2026</p><h2>Our approach</h2><p>STREAM AUTH is designed to help software teams manage authentication without collecting more data than is necessary. We process account, application, and authentication information solely to provide and improve the service.</p><h2>Information we process</h2><p>This may include account contact details, application configuration, license metadata, and limited device identifiers used for license policy enforcement. Customers control the end-user data they place in the platform.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can request access, correction, or deletion of your account information by contacting hello@streamauth.dev. We retain data only for as long as needed to operate the service and meet legal obligations.</p></article></BaseLayout>
